  "note": "Full unchanged measured-source XYZ, not independent surveys or accuracy ground truth. Native PLY input order is preserved; it is distinct from browser LOD indexing. Full-input production Delaunay TIN uses automatic edge rejection, with no extra thinning or transformed/generated coordinates. Independent archived native baseline supplies complete f64 distance bits, f64 statistics bits and scalar PLY oracle, then exits before timing. Separate archived baseline/candidate contexts share identical TIN, 4096-point original Morton chunks and fixed Rayon thread count. Each timed whole native cloud_to_mesh_par includes fresh BVH build, query ordering, parallel searches, result join and BVH destruction. No retained geometry/BVH across calls. Both builds adopt native scratch reuse, cached traversal bounds and indexed preparation. Candidate scans mesh coordinates once and admits only finite nonzero coordinates. It computes original bounds at leaves, then merges exact child min/max values for internal nodes instead of rescanning triangle vertices at every level. Zero/signed-zero/nonfinite meshes keep the preceding full scans to preserve target-dependent tie bits. Centroid reductions, axis selection, unstable partitions, preorder node IDs, triangle order, capacities, query chunks/guesses/missing-hit recovery and distance arithmetic remain unchanged. No new node buffer, persistent geometry/query/result cache or GPU dispatch is introduced. Shared core implementation also supports builds without the parallel feature; these timings measure only the native parallel API. No peak process memory guarantee is made. Loading/meshing/thread-pool construction, first use, five alternating warmups, f64/summary/PLY serialization/verification and cleanup are excluded. Ten alternating timed pairs are retained without outlier removal. No builds/tests/scans/edits alongside timing. Source, executable, script, input/manifest/original PCD hashes are checked before/after. Clocks/power/scheduling/other apps/allocator/code layout/pages uncontrolled. No Python conversion, browser RPC, WASM, GPU or isolated traversal speedup claim. No GPU model identifiers collected."
